# Production environment for the customer app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPLATE — committed. Real values are not.
#
# Where the real values go:
#   Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
#
# Set them per environment (Production / Preview / Development). Vite inlines
# these at BUILD time, not at runtime, so changing a value requires a redeploy
# — editing it in the dashboard does nothing until the next build.
#
# The Vercel projects already carry NEXT_PUBLIC_*/VERCEL_* variables; these are
# the ones this app needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The deployed API, INCLUDING the /api path segment.
#   Production: https://asian-taste-api.fly.dev/api
#
# Getting this wrong is a silent failure rather than a loud one: pointing at a
# bare origin makes every request 404 while the UI still renders. src/api/client.ts
# guards against it by appending /api and logging a warning, but set it right.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Stripe PUBLISHABLE key (pk_live_... for real payments, pk_test_... to test
# the checkout flow). Safe to expose in frontend code — it is the key the
# browser uses to tokenise card details.
#
# The SECRET key (sk_...) must never appear here or anywhere in this app.
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
